A config-declared macro is really executed: its argv runs as a subprocess and the
stripped output lands typed — echo of 1 lands unquoted as an integer.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Probe plan
---

Body.
-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  macros:
    probe:
      command: [echo, "1"]
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md answer="{{ macro('core.macros.probe') }}"
-- stdout --
--- plan.md
+++ plan.md
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 ---
 title: Probe plan
+answer: 1
 ---
 
 Body.
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: answer=1
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Probe plan
answer: 1
---

Body.
-- exit --
0
